INSERT INTO article_matchups (id, article_id, position, slot_label, away_team_name, home_team_name, away_record, home_record, line, away_score, home_score, body)
VALUES
  ('6a900e10-b7c2-4dc1-856e-ac90b87b465c', '91a8c7dc-2f2e-49ba-96cc-54ec0e375030', 1, 'TNF (AMZN)', 'Indian DJ', 'Maye I Digg in yo Boutte', '2-5', '2-5', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'On TNF, Indian DJ makes the very short trip to Carter-Finley Stadium to take on his cross-town opponent Maye I dig in yo Boutte in a matchup of this seasons bottom-dwellers.

TJ is sitting at 2-5 having watched his team lose five games in a row and it is leading him in a potential downward spiral.Yeah, Rashee Rice is back and looked like he never left and JSN continues to do his thing, but congrats bro – having two guys show up while the rest of your roster takes a collective shit is like being the best player on the Jets. Nobody cares.

Maye I dig in yo Boutte finally remembered how to win football games after starting 0-5 and is riding a 2 game winning steak and the second highest point total of the week coming into this matchup. The receiver room is stacked with the return of CeeDee Lamb and he looks like a potential sleeper playoff team if he can keep it going which would be one of the all time Bengals turnarounds considering he spent the first month and a half getting his ass spanked (Joseph try to hold in your excitement reading those words)'),
  ('825b3b85-fccb-4ef2-9f45-cbdc9963d152', '91a8c7dc-2f2e-49ba-96cc-54ec0e375030', 2, '1:00 PM (CBS)', 'Stevenson and White Guys', 'It Hurts a little', '2-5', '5-2', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Stevenson and White Guys returns home to Cary for a matchup at the historical Diwali grounds at Koka Booth Amphitheater

Alvin''s season is currently doing its best Titanic impression except instead of goin to the lifeboats everyone is just thuggin it out. Sitting at 2-5 in 10th place, and now the odds on favorite to get last, this man is speedrunning his way to last place like it''s a goddamn achievement. While talented pieces remain on this roster with guys like Achane and Olave, the guy is suffering from the fact that he rolls out Jerry Jeudy every week.

Meanwhile, Rishi''s at 5-2 in 2nd place, hunting for his FIRST Bengals championship (emphasis on the first championship). The perennial loser is playing this season with a sense of anger and he looks to continue that this week hoping that last weeks showing for the Eagles stack of Hurts and Smitty is here to stay.

Surely Rishi is able to keep is foot on the pedal and move to 6-2 against the faltering Alvin but we have seen, on any given week in the Cary Bengals league, anything can happen.'),
  ('4f8e2e54-2204-49d9-abfd-f3fa349892ae', '91a8c7dc-2f2e-49ba-96cc-54ec0e375030', 3, '12:00 PM (FOX)', 'Heterophobes Reloaded', 'Jayden Jefferson Jr’s Mom', '3-4', '3-4', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Heterophobes Reloaded make the trip to Wake County to take on Jayden Jefferson Jr’s Mom in an important matchup

Joseph is doing what it does best which is collapsing right on schedule and spreading his cheeks to whoever is on his schedule this time of year. Sitting at 3-4 in 7th, this team had its moment in the sun reaching the top of the power rankings and promptly bursting into flames. But wait, there''s a glimmer of hope! The return of Lamar Jackson and other guys getting healthy means Joseph might postpone a potential return to still life glory.

For Cotbib, he is experiencing what many expected may happen. The Linsanity run is over, the hot streak died, reality set in, and now he''s also 3-4 in 8th place watching his dreams disappear faster than the UNC’s football hopes after that opening drive against TCU. How do we know the Linsanity run is over? Justice Hill. That''s Carter''s RB1. Let that sink in. Justice. Hill. Enough said.'),
  ('90809ba7-7c6f-45f4-b570-dae609ad85c3', '91a8c7dc-2f2e-49ba-96cc-54ec0e375030', 4, '4:25 pm (FOX)', 'Nangali’s Naners', 'Code Monkey (PR #414)', '3-4', '5-2', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'In America''s game of the week, the Code Monkey welcomes Nangali’s Naners to the Frozen Tundra.

Samvit has assembled a roster that should be dominating – Dak, James Cook, ARSB, the whole damn crew. On paper, this team fucks. In reality he is 3-4 in 6th place and potentially staring down the barrel of another year without making playoffs. Not once. Never. Not a single goddamn time has this man experienced playoff fantasy football, and at this point it''s gotta be a curse. Can he break the curse and get a huge win this week while missing Amon-Ra St. Brown or does the playoff journey get tougher for a much maligned owner. Let’s see how it works this week for him playing a double TE combo of Kittle and Ertz which will be one of the most daring strategies of the year.

On the other side, Ankith''s reformed draft model has him sitting pretty at 5-2 in 1st place, fresh off damn near breaking the league''s weekly scoring record. This man is on a mission but doubt deservedly remains because the shitter finished last place twice which is one of the achievements of all time so the idea of him being a winner is a foreign concept. With CMC and JT, the Code Monkey feels he can win any matchup.'),
  ('cae80b76-d89a-463b-8107-28e991ff7414', '91a8c7dc-2f2e-49ba-96cc-54ec0e375030', 5, 'SNF (NBC)', 'Bark for Daddy!🫵🐶', 'Kamara vs the World', '5-2', '5-2', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'In a top of the table battle, Bark for Daddy!🫵🐶will leave the bright lights of civilization to travel to bumfuck cornfields in West Lafayette, Indiana to take on Kamara vs the World.

Kirk is somehow 5-2 and in 4th place, which is absolutely wild considering this man literally forgot to set his lineup last week. Word on the street is he was too busy with some French woman to check his fantasy team, and somehow he''s STILL winning games which has some aura if we are being honestt. Patrick Mahomes and Cam Skattebo are carrying this fraud to the promised land while Kirk''s off eating croissants and pretending to understand French cinema. It’ll be important to see if old man Flacco can establish a Tee Higgins resurgence for the knockoff Capital One bank guy.

Amogh is also 5-2 in 3rd, but unlike Kirk, he''s actually been paying attention. Problem is, Puka Nacua is on bye this week, and his stars aren''t necessarily starring as Rome Odunze has been trending downward, and Alvin Kamara''s recent stretch has me thinking he has been hanging around the wrong New Orleans crowd (Zion Williamson at Burger King).

Only one can move to 6-2 here with the hopes of getting one win closer to the all-important first round bye.'),
  ('e017a559-0b13-4c9e-9711-d7a1dc5d55cc', '91a8c7dc-2f2e-49ba-96cc-54ec0e375030', 6, 'MNF(ESPN)', 'Smooth Jazz w Kenny G', 'Tet Offensive', '4-3', '3-4', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'In a clash of Wolfpack alums, Smooth Jazz w Kenny G travels to Kenan Memorial Stadium to take on Tet Offensive in a Monday night showdown being labeled “The Child Sacrificers Bowl”.

Keshav is 4-3 in 5th, and this man has been playing with forces beyond our comprehension. He may have pulled a book out of the Sparsh playbook to make some things work but after the masses were calling him ass he has now won three in a row with some Mickey Mouse 0 RB strategy. It remains to be seen how long this bullshit can last but for now he at least can feel comfortable having Josh Allen and Chase who looks to be back with Flacco at QB.

Sparsh sits at 3-4 in 9th, and for a man who''s won multiple championships through what can only be described as ritualistic child sacrifice, karma''s finally catching up. His RB room is literally empty – Kenneth Walker III and Bam Knight are on bye, so he''s rolling out... nobody (as I write this)? The devil has forsaken him or maybe this is all part of some sick twisted plan. Whatever it is Sparsh has self described himself to be “locked out” this season but we know he just doesn’t know how to handle himself with things not going his way.

Sparsh has rings. Multiple. He''s been here before, sacrificed more kids than anyone, and built a dynasty on the bones of children. But this he''s probably getting his ass beat by a guy whose entire strategy was “dudes finna get hurt and then I can play their backups."')
ON CONFLICT (article_id, position) DO NOTHING;

